  "body": "This 411m² home has just been majorly renovated.\r\nSolid concrete and brick (not plaster).\r\nResource Consent approved to build an additional home.\r\n\r\nPositioned in one of St Heliers’ most sought-after streets, this substantial residence has undergone a major modernisation — delivering the look and feel of a near-new home, while retaining its original concrete exterior that has already withstood the test of time.\r\n\r\nA soaring timber ceiling crowns the large open-plan living area, anchored by a premium granite kitchen with scullery and opening onto a large entertainers deck with forested outlook. Accommodation is also generous and highly flexible. The master suite offers a private retreat with bespoke dressing room and luxurious ensuite, supported by three additional executive bathrooms. Currently configured with a self-contained apartment for additional income or multi-generational family living, the home can easily function as a five or even six-bedroom residence.\r\n\r\nA swimming pool, separate swim spa, level grounds, and secure four-car garaging complete the offering.\r\n\r\nAdding to its appeal is the future upside. With Resource Consent already approved for an additional family home on the front — presenting a clear opportunity to add further value. This rare combination may also appeal to purchasers exploring opportunities under the Active Investor Plus (AIP) category (subject to independent advice).\r\n\r\nMoments from St Heliers village and the waterfront, this is a property defined by scale, opportunities and long-term value — a smarter alternative to buying new.",
